  "raw": {
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020054": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Regional and Urban Planning, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 Assistant Professor in Regional and Urban Planning, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Assistant Professor in Regional and Urban Planning within UCD School of Architecture The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in shaping the future direction of the planning unit at UCD. We welcome applications from outstanding scholars who can either consolidate and deepen our current institutional specialisms or expand our expertise into emerging, innovative fields. Areas may include but are not limited to: Major Infrastructure Planning and Delivery; Energy Planning and Climate Change; Spatial & Environmental Justice; Smart Cities & Digital Technologies: Sustainable Mobility & Transport Planning; Housing Dynamics; and Urban & Regional Economic Development. The successful candidate will deliver and develop curriculum for undergraduate and postgraduate planning programmes, including PhD supervision and will develop an internationally renowned research profile through high-impact publications and major external grant acquisition. Note for Applicants Particular to this position: As part of their application, applicants are requested to submit: A cover letter, which includes a teaching statement, outlining their teaching experience, teaching and learning philosophy, and planned approach to teaching and module development, and a research statement, outlining their research plans. This should be 3 A4 pages maximum (using Arial 10pt font at 1.5 line spacing, with all margins at 2.54 cm). 95 Lecturer/Asst. Professor (Above The Bar)_2010 (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020056": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Economics (Environmental Economics), UCD School of Economics, Permanent (commencing 1st August 2027)",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Economics (Environmental Economics), UCD School of Economics, Permanent (commencing 1st August 2027) Applications are invited for a permanent post of an Associate Professor in Economics (Environmental Economics) within UCD School of Economics. Applicants must have an active research track record and be an effective communicator capable of excellence in teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The successful applicant will be expected to teach (but not exclusively) on UCD’s BSc in Sustainability. Applications from relevant fields such as Environmental Economics, Energy Economics, Climate Change are welcomed. 95 Associate Professor (7941) €85,864 - €121,260 per annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020053": {
      "title": "Associate Professor OR Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Medicinal Chemistry and Chemical Biology, UCD School of Chemistry, Permanent",
      "description": "Associate Professor OR Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Medicinal Chemistry and Chemical Biology, UCD School of Chemistry, Permanent **Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Associate Professor OR Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Medicinal Chemistry and Chemical Biology within UCD School of Chemistry.** The person appointed will be expected to become a leading figure within Ireland’s Medicinal Chemistry & Chemical Biology community, sustain an internationally recognised research team, and interact with other disciplinary areas within the University. The appointee will also be expected to take full advantage of large-scale national research funding opportunities (for example, through Research Ireland), and potential research funding streams available through the European Union and other international agencies. Entry to UCD Science programmes is highly competitive and we attract talented students from Ireland and abroad. The School delivers three BSc programmes (Chemistry, Chemistry with Environmental and Sustainable Chemistry, and Medicinal Chemistry and Chemical Biology). The latter is currently the largest BSc major in the College of Science, and the successful candidate will play an important role in the development and delivery of the latter. In addition, we contribute courses to several other Schools, and postgraduate-level courses to our taught MSc and structured PhD programmes. 95 Associate Professor_2010 Salary Scale: €85,864 - €121,260 per annum Or 95 Lecturer/Assistant Professor (Above The Bar): €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 30/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020121": {
      "title": "Chief Information Security Officer (CISO), UCD IT Services, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Chief Information Security Officer (CISO), UCD IT Services, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) within UCD IT Services. Technology is playing an increasingly vital role amid these times of change and growth. In UCD, the digital campus is recognised as having equal importance as the physical campus. UCD’s digital landscape underpins and supports the university’s critical teaching, research and administrative operations, and is also a key enabler in the successful delivery of UCD’s strategic initiatives. 95 Snr Administrative Ii_2013 (2010) Salary: €112,235 - €150,022 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. _____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Príomhoifigeach Slándála Faisnéise (CISO) laistigh de Seirbhísí TF UCD. Tá ról ríthábhachtach ag an teicneolaíocht sa lá atá inniu ann. In UCD, aithnítear anois go bhfuil an campas digiteach chomh tábhachtach céanna leis an gcampas fisiciúil. Braitheann tacaíocht do theagasc, taighde agus riarachán in UCD go mór ar thimpeallacht dhigiteach láidir, atá mar bhunús chun cuspóirí straitéiseacha na hollscoile a bhaint amach. 95 Snr Administrative Ii_2013 (2010) Scála Tuarastail: €112,235 - €150,022 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 27/10/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. < #UCDITS >"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020129": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Project Manager, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 12 Months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Clinical Research Project Manager, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 12 Months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Clinical Research Project Manager within UCD School of Medicine. The UCD CRC was established in 2006 to deliver high quality, world class, patient-centered research. Together with our hospital partners and the UCD School of Medicine, we have built a skilled and committed research team who help investigators to design and conduct clinical research to the highest standards. Fixed Salary: €55,000 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 21st October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020067": {
      "title": "Consultant Psychiatrist, UCD Student Health Service, Temporary 3 year, Part time 0.6 FTE",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 Consultant Psychiatrist, UCD Student Health Service, Temporary 3 year, Part time 0.6 FTE Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.6 FTE) post of a Consultant Psychiatrist within UCD Student Health Service. As part of the Student Health Service team, the psychiatrist will provide a service focused on the needs of the Student Population. The service is complementary to community psychiatry services and responsibility for the provision of psychiatry rests primarily with multidisciplinary teams within the HSE. When appropriate and necessary the psychiatrist will liaise with community mental health services to arrange for the management of students with more complex needs. Reporting to the Director of Student Health, the psychiatrist will demonstrate the ability to autonomously manage their own patient caseload. The successful psychiatrist will work with the UCD general practitioners, and other UCD Student Health Service team members to provide and manage effective professional and efficient clinical services. 95 Senior Administrative Officer 1 _2013 (2010) (7952) Salary Scale: €147,198 - €186,094 Per Annum Pro Rata Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach páirtaimseartha (0.6 FTE) Síciatraí Comhairleach laistigh de Seirbhís Sláinte na Mac Léinn. Agus iad ag obair laistigh d'fhoireann na Seirbhíse Sláinte na Mac Léinn, cuireann an síciatraí cúram ar fáil a dhíríonn ar riachtanais dhaonra na mac léinn. Oibríonn an tseirbhís seo i gcomhar le soláthar sláinte meabhrach pobail, áit a bhfanann an phríomhfhreagracht as cúram síciatrach le foirne ildisciplíneacha an FSS. Nuair is iomchuí agus is gá, comhoibríonn an síciatraí leis na foirne pobail seo chun socruithe a dhéanamh maidir le bainistíocht mac léinn a bhfuil riachtanais níos casta acu. Ag tuairisciú do Stiúrthóir Sláinte na Mac Léinn, léireoidh an síciatraí cumas láidir a léiriú maidir lena n-ualach cásanna othar féin a bhainistiú go neamhspleách. Oibreoidh an síciatraí a cheapfar i gcomhar le dochtúirí teaghlaigh UCD agus foireann níos leithne na Seirbhíse Sláinte chun seirbhísí cliniciúla éifeachtacha agus gairmiúla a sholáthar agus a bhainistiú. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 15 Mí Deireadh Fomhair 2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020117": {
      "title": "Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science / CeADAR, Temporary Until 30th June 2027",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science / CeADAR, Temporary Until 30th June 2027 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Data Scientist II within the School of Computer Science / CeADAR Applications are invited for the role of Data Scientist II in CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI. CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. We are very passionate about applying ML algorithms and develop AI applied research and innovation solutions using classic ML to novel transformer neural networks. We test and measure the real customer impact of each model we deploy and support the ecosystem with training, advisory, and AI infrastructure. CeADAR is seeking an experienced individual who will support applied research projects and who have a demonstrated successful track record in data science in industrial research settings (>2 years). Salary range: €55,000 to €70,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020114": {
