      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science CeADAR, Temporary 3 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Data Scientist II within UCD School of Computer Science CeADAR CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. CeADAR is seeking an experienced individual who has a demonstrated successful track record in applied data science. Salary Range: €55,000 - €70,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9-Oct.-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
