    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020105": {
      "title": "Director of Digital Strategy, Office of Registrar and Deputy President, Temporary 3 Year Fixed Term",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Director of Digital Strategy, Office of Registrar and Deputy President, Temporary 3 Year Fixed Term Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Director of Digital Strategy within the Office of Registrar and Deputy President. Following a strategic review of executive capacity in digital development, University College Dublin (UCD) has established a leadership role positioned within the portfolio of the Registrar. Operating at the intersection of digital innovation, technology architecture, and institutional vision, the Director of Digital Strategy provides dedicated leadership capacity and expertise to design, drive, and embed a comprehensive, multi-year digital roadmap across the University to meet the ambitions set out in the UCD Breaking Boundaries Strategy. This role works in close strategic partnership with the Chief Information Officer, the UCD Strategy Office and executive leadership. The Director of Digital Strategy will be a visionary and influential leader, who shapes university-wide digital direction, aligns cross-departmental priorities, and prepares academic and administrative units for digital transformation. This strategic mandate works in direct support of the CIO's remit by securing institutional consensus through collaboration, clarifying business demand, driving and fostering digital adoption and adaptation, whilst creating the environment needed to support our digital roadmap. Salary Scale: 95 Snr Administrative I_2013 (2010) (7952) : €147,198 - €186,094 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020106": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, UCD Human Resource (HRIS), 11 Months (Temporary part-time at 0.4fte)",
      "description": "Executive Assistant, UCD Human Resource (HRIS), 11 Months (Temporary part-time at 0.4fte) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Executive Assistant within UCD Human Resource (HRIS). The HRIS Executive Assistant will be a member of UCD Human Resources Services working within the HRIS Team. Applicants must have the ability to multi-task, meet deadlines and be able to maintain a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail in completing their work. They must have proven communication, administrative and organisational skills. The person will also contribute to the process of continuous improvement within HRIS as well as contributing to project work and any other duties as directed by the Senior HRIS Analyst. 95 Executive Assistant_2013 (7911) €32,856 - €49,419 at 0.4fte pro rata. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 14/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Cúntóir Feidhmiúcháin laistigh de HRIS. Ní mór do na hiarrthóirí cumais láidre eagrúcháin, riaracháin agus cumarsáide a bheith acu, agus taithí acu ar iltascanna a dhéanamh, spriocdhátaí dochta a bhainistiú, agus cruinneas agus aird ar mhionsonraí den scoth a choinneáil. Baineann an ról le cur le tionscnaimh feabhsúcháin leanúnaigh HRIS, tacú le hobair thionscadail, agus dualgais bhreise a chomhlíonadh de réir mar a iarrann an tAnailísí Sinsearach HRIS. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 14/10/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020127": {
      "title": "I-C3 Venture Manager, NovaUCD, Fixed term post until 30th June 2029",
      "description": "I-C3 Venture Manager, NovaUCD, Fixed term post until 30th June 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a I-C3 Venture Manager within NovaUCD The I-C3 Venture Partner is a highly strategic and hands-on commercial development role, integral to the I-C3 (Ireland's Chips Competence Centre) project. The purpose and objective of the ‘I-C3 Project’ is to establish Ireland's dedicated Chips Competence Centre to accelerate the commercial scale-up of Irish semiconductor deep-tech companies by providing them with access to advanced infrastructure, expertise, and critical private and public funding to strengthen the nation's and Europe's strategic autonomy in microelectronics. The I-C3 consortium includes UCD, Tyndall Institute, MCCI and MIDAS. Salary: €70,000 - €100,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 21/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020130": {
      "title": "IT Systems Manager, UCD IT Services, Specified Purpose, Until May 2031 (with 6 month panel for future permanent and temporary roles)",
      "description": "IT Systems Manager, UCD IT Services, Specified Purpose, Until May 2031 (with 6 month panel for future permanent and temporary roles) Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a IT Systems Manager within UCD IT Services. Applications are invited for the role of IT Systems Manager in the Infrastructure Team. The IT Systems Manager will be responsible for leading an operational IT team in delivering critical IT services to the UCD community. The role will include managing technical projects, evaluating, developing and implementing new technology and software within the University. The successful candidate will also be expected to assist with the design and management of Infrastructure solutions both on-premise and in the cloud and daily operational facets of the UCD IT Systems, Storage and Data Centres. A key role for the IT Systems Manager is the ability to effectively communicate complex, technical issues to a wide and varied audience and interact with senior management within the University as required. The role involves dealing with a wide range of complicated technologies and will require knowledge, experience and first-hand involvement in the provision and support of Systems, Storage and Data Centres. Reporting to the CIO or their nominee, the postholder will be responsible for a substantial programme of work, comprising multiple major projects and technical development initiatives. 95 Admin Off Ia_2013 (2010) Salary: €72,750 - €85,012 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 28/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. < #UCDITS > Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post cuspóir sonraithe Bainisteoir Córais TF laistigh de Seirbhísí TF UCD. Tá ról ríthábhachtach ag an teicneolaíocht maidir le dul chun cinn agus nuálaíocht a chur chun cinn ar fud na hollscoile. In UCD, aithnítear anois go bhfuil an campas digiteach chomh tábhachtach céanna leis an gcampas fisiciúil. Tá freagracht ar Sheirbhísí TF UCD as dearadh, forbairt, cur i bhfeidhm, bainistíocht agus tacaíocht a dhéanamh do raon leathan réiteach agus seirbhísí TF chun tacú leis an bhfoireann, leis na mic léinn agus leis na taighdeoirí ina gcuid oibre don Ollscoil. Cuireann Seirbhísí TF UCD gach feidhmchlár, tacaíocht agus bonneagar lárnach TF ar fáil ar fud na hOllscoile. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 28/10/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020060": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Assistant Professor (above the bar) in post-1945 history of war, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose Cover (approximately 5 Years)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Lecturer / Assistant Professor (above the bar) in post-1945 history of war, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose Cover (approximately 5 Years) Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer / Assistant Professor (above the bar) in post-1945 history of war within the School of History The School of History is seeking to appoint a Specified Purpose cover (estimated duration 5-years) Lecturer in the history of war post-1945, ideally with a focus on Europe (including Northern Ireland / Britain and decolonisation conflicts). The expected start date is 1 January 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing these teaching initiatives and pursue their own research projects. The successful candidate will: o teach survey and research-led modules at BA level, including co-teaching a second-year survey module on twentieth-century war; o contribute to the MA in International War Studies; o supervise undergraduate and graduate dissertations; o contribute to the administration of the School, as designated by the Head of School; o have the opportunity to develop their research agenda and to apply for University and College seed-funding schemes; o pursue research, including peer-reviewed publications and grant applications; o Undertake other duties as assigned by the Head of School; o participate in student recruitment and internationalisation activities; Engage in appropriate Professional Development and other training programmes in the University; Promote the development of the School, College and the University; Maintain the highest professional standards to enhance School and University performance and reputation; Undertake such other duties as may be reasonably requested, commensurate with the nature and grade of the post. Salary Scale: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) €66,055 - € 104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 16 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020071": {
      "title": "Lecturer Assistant Professor in Economics, UCD School of Economics, Temporary Fixed Term 5-year post commencing 1st September 2027",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Lecturer Assistant Professor in Economics, UCD School of Economics, Temporary Fixed Term 5-year post commencing 1st September 2027 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer Assistant Professor in Economics within UCD School of Economics Applications are invited for positions as Lecturer/Assistant Professor in the UCD School of Economics. Applicants must have an active research track record and be an effective communicator capable of excellence in teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Applications from all fields of Economics are welcomed. Salary: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar €66,055 - € 104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020135": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter) Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production within the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science Applications are invited for the post of Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production. This role, based in the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, will support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, and wider engagement in the area of dairy production. The appointee will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team of 18 full-time academics within the Section of Animal & Crop Science, contributing to a shared mission of addressing global food, environmental, and societal challenges through teaching, research, and knowledge exchange in animal and crop production systems. We are seeking a highly motivated individual with a demonstrated passion for teaching and research in dairy production, with an emphasis on grass-based systems of production. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in Agricultural Science or a closely related discipline, with a strong focus on dairy production and ideally with research interests that intersect with grass and forage production and environmental sustainability. In addition to a strong research profile, the appointee should demonstrate excellent communication, organisational and interpersonal skills and a commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020097": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2) within UCD School of Politics and International Relations. The UCD School of Politics & International Relations (SPIRe) is a globally ranked, research-active school with teaching and research expertise across the fields of political science, international relations, normative political theory, international development, and other areas. It is committed to the highest standards in undergraduate and graduate teaching and research supervision. The school is home to a number of research centres, and further information can be found at: https://www.ucd.ie/spire/about/ 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9th November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020090": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History within the School of History The School of History is seeking to appoint a lecturer to a 1.5 year post in modern migration History. The School has recently expanded its teaching provision and research expertise in global and migration history. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing these teaching initiatives, pursue their own research projects and act as the academic lead on the School’s Summer School. The successful candidate will be expected to be in post for the 2026/27 Spring trimester (January 2027). Salary Scale: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) €66,055 - €104,600 Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020074": {
      "title": "Post Doc Research Fellow  Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Fixed Term until 28 February 2029",
      "description": "Post Doc Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Fixed Term until 28 February 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post Doc Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering The QUBIC project is a strategic initiative aimed at addressing critical challenges in high-impact sectors such as energy, advanced materials, and pharmaceutical discovery through advancing quantum computing. The project is funded by Enterprise Ireland through the Disruptive Technologies Innovation Fund (DTIF). The successful candidate will contribute to the “Quantum Computing for Power and Energy Systems” research stream. The aim is to establish tangible prospects for leveraging Quantum Computing to address the modern day computational and stochastic challenges of electrical power system planning and operation. The dual goal is to tap into the current capabilities of Quantum Computing while also streamlining the future exploitation of further advancements in the field. Research activities will be carried out within an interdisciplinary team of UCD researchers working on QUBIC across Electrical Power Systems and Quantum Computing, providing opportunities for close collaboration and upskilling across the two domains. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum or €55,399 - €58,578 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020137": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 12 months post",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 12 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering. This project aims to leverage the power of artificial intelligence (AI) to enhance the efficiency of a plastic pretreatment framework that integrates advanced sensing technologies, process modelling, and optimisation strategies, thereby rendering plastic waste more suitable for microbial fermentation. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 16/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020124": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Civil Engineering. The candidate will be involved with implementing high temporal resolution sampling strategies of key parameters (and proxy/ surrogate parameters) across selected study sites that reflect a full range of catchment pressures. In addition, the successful candidate will implement approaches to assess hydromorphological condition (or changes in condition) at these selected study sites. Event based sampling, where pollution releases will be at their highest will be systematically targeted. The candidate will analyse collected data and model studied catchments to inform more rapid and better decision making in the context of a pressure-stressor-response conceptual framework that will be explored. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020077": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Geography,  24 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Geography, 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1within UCD School of Geography. MigHealthGaps is an European Research Council (ERC)-funded project led by Associate Professor Silvia Loi, that investigates health disparities and healthy aging trajectories between immigrants and non-immigrants. The core research objectives of the project are: measure health and aging trajectories of immigrants by age, gender, and socioeconomic status across European countries, as compared to non-immigrants; analyse how family composition and ties impact or mitigate these health gaps; identify specific socioeconomic shocks or life circumstances that divert immigrants onto poorer aging trajectories. This is an academic research role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Salary: €47,273- €53,925 per annum . Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020136": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Psychology. Applications are invited from suitably qualified candidates for a full-time, fixed term position as a Postdoctoral Researcher with the School of Psychology, in collaboration with Jigsaw-The National Centre for Youth Mental Health. This position is funded by the Health Research Board (HRB) and is available from November 2026 until November 2029. Salary Scale: Post Doc Level 1 €47,273 - €52,513 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020118": {
      "title": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts",
      "description": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Bainisteoir Imeachtaí Aitheantais laistigh de Clárlann UCD – Imeachtaí Earcaíochta agus Aitheantais Mac Léinn Cuireann Clárlann UCD réimse leathan seirbhísí riaracháin acadúla agus mac léinn ar fáil. Díríonn a misean ar sheirbhísí gairmiúla, treoir agus tacaíocht den scoth atá dírithe ar an mac léinn a fhorbairt agus a sholáthar do mhic léinn ionchasacha, do mhic léinn reatha, d’iar-mhic léinn, do bhaill foirne acadúla agus do bhaill foirne gairmiúla i ngach céim de shaolré mac léinn na hollscoile. Scála Tuarastail: €72,750 - €85,012 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 19/10/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Recognition Events Manager within UCD Registry – Student Recruitment & Recognition Events UCD Registry delivers a broad range of student and academic administrative services, whose mission is to develop and deliver the highest quality student-centred professional services, support and advice to prospective students, current students, alumni, faculty and professional staff in respect of the key administrative functions relating to a student's life cycle in the University. Salary: 95 Admin Off Ia_2013 (2010) (7080) €72,750 - €85,012 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020076": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 7-month part-time post i.e. 0.2fte",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 7-month part-time post i.e. 0.2fte Applications are invited for a temporary part time post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering The aim of this project is to create a scalable and transferable blueprint for digital pre-laboratory training resources, co-created with learners and new laboratory users. These resources will complement face-to-face training for a consistent, efficient, and inclusive student induction experience. Salary Range: €34,129 - €42,173 per annum, pro-rata 0.2 fte Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020132": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary Part-Time (0.8fte) Post for 12 Months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary Part-Time (0.8fte) Post for 12 Months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within the School of Biosystems and Food Engineering BIOSPARK will be a game-changer for Europe’s skills and capacity in circular bio-based systems. Building on BIObec, the EBU Alliance, and BIOEAST UniNet, it will create a pan-European network of 27 Bio-Based Education Centres (BBECs) covering all EU-27, serving as regional anchors for education, training, and mutual learning, and together forming a European reference hub for bioeconomy and circularity skills. The project tackles urgent needs: fragmented training frameworks, shortage of skilled professionals, limited inclusion of Widening countries, and weak academia–industry collaboration. BIOSPARK adopts a systemic, multi-actor approach, engaging the quadruple helix to co-create and deploy curricula, training actions, and lifelong learning pathways. Its work unfolds in four phases: setting-up, shaping, piloting, and strengthening. This research assistant position will support the project objectives, especially on monitoring and assessment of curricula actions. Fixed Salary: €34,129 per annum, pro-rata (equal to €27,303 per annum part-time, at 0.8te) Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020125": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Until 30 June 2027",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Until 30 June 2027 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR. CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. We are very passionate about applying ML algorithms and develop AI applied research and innovation solutions using from classic ML to novel transformer neural networks. We test and measure the real customer impact of each model we deploy and support the ecosystem with training, advisory, and AI infrastructure. This is an exciting opportunity as CeADAR is expanding and has a number of diverse and exciting projects in the area of data science with real application to a variety of verticals in the industry sector both at national and EU level, including the start-up ecosystem. Initially, the selected candidate will work on the AI2Peat project. More about the project: AI2Peat – All-Ireland, AI enhanced Peatland Monitoring Platform – is a project funded by Research Ireland (Future Digital Challenge). Its consortium is composed of CeADAR – Ireland’s centre for applied AI; iCRAG – the SFI centre in applied geosciences; and the Irish NPWS – National Parks and Wildlife Service. AI2Peat leverages remote sensing, artificial intelligence (AI) and Geographical Information Systems (GIS), along with domain expert knowledge from the field, to assess and continually monitor Ireland’s peatland condition in a structured and resilient manner. AI2Peat is a project that aims to have significant societal impact, and so its design is informed by a continuous interdisciplinary and cross-community stakeholder engagement. The work outputs will be deployed on PeatSense, a platform designed to contribute to the monitoring, restoration and conservation of peatlands in Ireland (and beyond). Research Assistant Salary Range: €34,129 - €44,311 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020116": {
      "title": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months",
      "description": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Business Development Manager within UCD School of Economics. Rinn Energy is a national, co-led research centre funded by Research Ireland (Taighde Éireann), bringing together a consortium of leading universities and partners to deliver internationally leading, interdisciplinary research to support the transition to a low-carbon, secure, and resilient energy system. The Centre seeks to appoint a Business Development Manager (BDM) to successfully build collaborative research relationships between our world-leading academics and industry. The role requires identifying new industry members, projects, and training opportunities while maintaining a significant understanding of academic capabilities and industry requirements. The successful candidate will develop a portfolio of fully funded and co-funded collaborative research projects, with success measured directly by increased industry investment in the centre. Salary Scale: €88,000 - €105,000 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020101": {
      "title": "Research Coordinator, UCD Sutherland School of Law, Fixed term until 29 December 2029",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 Research Coordinator, UCD Sutherland School of Law, Fixed term until 29 December 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Coordinator within UCD Sutherland School of Law. Applications are invited for a Research Coordinator and Administrator position on a part-time basis (full-time) for a fixed-term period of 3 years, with a possible extension. The position supports two ERC projects within the UCD Sutherland School of Law (two days per week on each project), and convening attached to the Chair in Global Refugee and Migration Law and related centre-building activities. Project 1 is an ERC Consolidator Grant led by Professor Aisling Swaine (Principal Investigator). The ‘GENCOERCTRL project’ is a qualitative study focused on women’s experiences of armed group violence and responses by transitional justice processes. The role will provide research coordination, project management, administration and recruitment support to ensure the effective delivery of the project, alongside the Principal Investigator, Professor Aisling Swaine and team of researchers. Project 2 relates to an ERC Consolidator Grant led by Professor Cathryn Costello (Principal Investigator), a global comparative study of the effectiveness of international refugee law, using both quantitative and qualitative methods. The third aspect includes to a set of activities broadly in the field of international law and global justice led by Professor Cathryn Costello, with the aim of developing UCD as a centre of excellence in this field. The role will provide key support for research projects, events, networking and institution-building both within and outside UCD in this field. The Research Coordinator and Administrator will manage both projects, following a project management approach including clear structures, workflows, planning milestones, progress assessment, and all tasks related to financial and narrative oversight and reporting. They will deal with all administrative matters relating to both projects, team members and external collaborators. This will include dealing with external vendors, file and data management systems, reporting and meeting schedules, GDPR compliance and other daily administrative tasks. The Research Coordinator and Administrator will support the organisation of conferences and workshops and public dissemination, including social media and websites. The role will be a key point of contact for each project team. We are looking for a person with a qualification in project management and/or administration with excellent communication, planning, financial and project oversight skills, including across different cultures. You will have competency in working closely with different departments of the university to ensure that the projects can each effectively avail of support available within and beyond the College. Fixed Salary: €41,000 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020091": {
      "title": "Research Ethics Advisor, UCD Research, Office of Research Ethics, 5 years (Panel 6 months Temporary posts)",
      "description": "Research Ethics Advisor, UCD Research, Office of Research Ethics, 5 years (Panel 6 months Temporary posts) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Ethics Advisor within UCD Research, Office of Research Ethics. Under the direction of the Research Ethics Officer, the successful candidate will be a key member of the Office of Research Ethics, providing advice and support to the wider university community, as part of the Research Integrated Services (RIS) Strategic Initiative, as well as assisting with the administrative support to the office. The key responsibilities will be to assist and advise Principal Investigators and researchers in preparing and submitting ethics applications involving human participants, to the university's Human Research Ethics Committee – Sciences (HREC-LS) or Human Research Ethics Committee – Humanities (HREC HS). In addition, the successful candidate will develop and update new research ethics guidelines as necessary. The post holder will play a role in delivering UCD Strategic Initiatives by providing a researcher-centric support for research ethics submissions. 95 Admin Officer Ii_2010 (0173_X) €52,519 - €67,129 per annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Comhairleoir Eitice Taighde laistigh de Taighde UCD, Oifig Eitice Taighde. Ag feidhmiú faoi threoir an Oifigigh Eitice Taighde, beidh ról lárnach ag an té a cheapfar san Oifig Eitice Taighde. Mar chuid de Thionscnamh Straitéiseach na Seirbhísí Comhtháite Taighde (RIS), cuirfidh sealbhóir an phoist comhairle agus tacaíocht ar fáil do phobal na hollscoile agus cabhróidh siad freisin le tacaíocht riaracháin a chur ar fáil don oifig. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 15/10/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020119": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The EVEREST project is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Staff Exchange (MSCA SE) funded under Horizon Europe, focused on cutting-edge research into extracellular vesicles (EVs) for innovative diagnostic and therapeutic applications in oncology, cardiovascular, and neurodegenerative diseases. The Research Project Manager will play a key role in managing the project across its multiple partners in multiple countries, supporting the coordination of up to 285 months of secondments between academic and non-academic institutions. Salary: €40,000 - €50,000 per annum (€20,000 - €25,000 per annum pro rata) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020115": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics & Gynaecology (Coombe Hospital), UCD School of Medicine/Coombe Hospital, Temporary Specified Purpose for maternity cover circa 6 months",
      "description": "Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics & Gynaecology (Coombe Hospital), UCD School of Medicine/Coombe Hospital, Temporary Specified Purpose for maternity cover circa 6 months Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics & Gynaecology (Coombe Hospital) within UCD School of Medicine / Coombe Hospital. The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. A number of Clinical Tutors are also actively involved in our biomedical, clinical or medical education research working with a specific Principal Investigator and may be undertaking a higher research degree (e.g. MD, MCh, MAO, MSc or PhD). These individuals are responsible for undertaking research experiments or data reviews and disseminating their findings through publication as a thesis, in academic journals or at scientific meetings. All Clinical Tutors are part of a vibrant community of academic staff who pass on their clinical experience and expertise to the next generation of medical professionals. The School provides academic support and training such that the Tutors themselves develop their own educational expertise and leadership. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum . Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 16/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020131": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy within the School of Public Health Supporting the UCD Director of Clinical Education, Subject Head, Programme Director(s) and Practice Education Team to deliver high quality academic and practice placement education. This position is aligned with Physiotherapy . The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will support staff on practice placement sites and the UCD Practice Education Team to deliver high quality practice placement education. The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will also be available to support students virtually and/or in person if required by the UCD Practice Education Team. The appointee will contribute to module coordination and delivery for programmes offered by the school on-site in UCD and/or on-line where appropriate. The role will be based on site in UCD and/or on practice placement sites as directed by their line manager, with travel as required. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.5 FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020120": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.8 FTE) post of a Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy within UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy. The successful candidate will play a key role in the delivery and development of Environmental Policy teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate level, working across the Environmental Policy degree programmes to support high-quality, research-informed, policy-oriented, and experiential learning. The Teaching Fellow will contribute to the design, delivery and assessment of Environmental Policy modules, including through lectures, workshops, tutorials, project-based learning and other forms of skills-based teaching. In addition to the teaching duties, a particular focus of the role will be supporting module coordinators on modules with substantial student numbers, including teaching, administration and assessment of the modules. Overall, the Teaching Fellow will be expected to contribute to continuity of teaching provision across the Environmental Policy subject area. The post will have significant responsibilities in programme and student support, including module management, programme administration, management of online platforms, external-examiner support, supervision of postgraduate internships and research projects, as well as contributing to programme activities including orientation, careers and employer engagement. Fixed Salary: €49,500 Per Annum Pro-Rata (i.e. equal to €39,600 Per Annum, Part-time at 0.8 FTE) Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020059": {
      "title": "UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science Applications are invited for a very dynamic post-doctoral scientist to lead our Precision Nutrition, Obesity and Cancer Project within the Precision Oncology Ireland Programme (POI; https://www.precisiononcology.ie/) with Prof Helen Roche’s Nutrigenomics Team at UCD Conway Institute https://people.ucd.ie/helen.roche; in collaboration with Dr Martina Wallace and Dr Fiona McGillicdddy. POI, now in its second phase POI2, is a pioneering Irish consortium that brings together Irish universities, cancer charities, industry partners and healthcare providers to advance personalised cancer treatment. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020126": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 in Heterotrophic Microalgal Cultivation on Brewery Co-products, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 18 months, Full time 1.0 FTE",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 in Heterotrophic Microalgal Cultivation on Brewery Co-products, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 18 months, Full time 1.0 FTE Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 in Heterotrophic Microalgal Cultivation on Brewery Co-products within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering. Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Scientist to join the AlgaeBrew2Scale project at the UCD Algae Group. AlgaeBrew2Scale is developing a breakthrough technology that transforms brewery co-products into valuable biobased ingredients. This is a postdoctoral research position that involves the execution of a defined research programme under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. The successful candidate will focus on cultivation of heterotrophic microalgae on brewery co-products. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. The primary purpose of the role is to further develop your research skills and competences, including the processes of publication in peer-reviewed academic publications, the development of funding proposals, the mentorship of graduate students along with the opportunity to develop your skills in research led teaching. Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020095": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 24 Months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 24 Months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. Vision loss can result in significant loss of independence. For many people, vision loss is caused by disruptions to specialized cells in the retina, the layer at the back of the eye that detects light to generate images. This leads to the broad clinical term of retinal degeneration (RD) which encompasses inherited retinal degeneration (IRD), age-related macular degeneration (AMD) and diabetic retinopathy (DR).For RD patients, there remains a need to discover and develop better treatments that are more broadly effective within multiple affected patient populations. Thus, our approach is to start with understanding biological processes commonly changed in retinal degeneration. In particular, we chose to focus on exciting new targets called “extracellular vesicles” or EVs. These are small messengers released by cells in the retina and which can send unwanted signals to other cells, thus, initiating and supporting disease. In this research, our ambition is to document the cargo contained within these cellular messages in multiple scenarios of retinal degeneration. This will include patient samples and pre-clinical research models of retinal degeneration. This broad collection of samples will allow us to use state-of-the-art approaches to profile molecules (e.g. proteins) commonly present in retinal degeneration. Their role in mediating vision loss will be validated. This will identify disease pathways but also reveal targets for future therapeutics to ameliorate vision loss. PD1 Salary Scale: €47,879 – €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. PD2 Fixed Salary: €55,399 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020112": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary full time 1.0 FTE for 21 months post.",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary full time 1.0 FTE for 21 months post. Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within the School of Biosystems and Food Engineering Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Scientist role within the SusAlgaePro project at UCD Algae Group. SusAlgaePro aims to develop a breakthrough microalgal biorefinery platform that transforms industrial waste into lipid fractions for Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) and protein ingredients for animal feed. This is a postdoctoral research position that involves the execution of a defined research programme under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. The successful candidate will grow microalgae on digestate and apply the cascading biorefinery fractionation to the resulting fresh biomass to produce lipid and protein ingredients. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020110": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science. Applications are invited for a temporary, full-time position of Post-Doctoral Researcher in the UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, based in the Conway Institute. The lab is also linked with the FutureNeuro Research Centre (https://www.futureneurocentre.ie/). The successful applicant will work on a two-year research project exploring translational disruptions in mouse models of epilepsy. The postdoctoral researcher will use a combination of pharmacological and transgenic approaches, in vivo mouse models of epilepsy and molecular-based analyses to determine how altered translation contributes to epileptogenesis and seizure disorders. There will also be the opportunity for the researcher to explore and profile novel epitranscriptomic modifications in epilepsy. Examples of previous work can be found here: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=d2vwSvIAAAAJ&hl=en Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020111": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 3 months, Full time (1.0 FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary 3 months, Full time (1.0 FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering. Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Scientist role within the Micro-lysis project at UCD Algae Group. Micro-lysis aims to develop a breakthrough biorefinery platform that transforms fresh microalgal biomass into valuable lipid and protein ingredients This is a postdoctoral research position that involves the execution of a defined research programme under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. The successful candidate will characterise microalgal cell-wall structure and apply the resulting insights to optimise lipid and protein extraction from fresh biomass. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. The primary purpose of the role is to further develop your research skills and competences, including the processes of publication in peer-reviewed academic publications, the development of funding proposals, the mentorship of graduate students along with the opportunity to develop your skills in research led teaching. Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020133": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 Oct. 2028 (Commencing 4 January 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 Oct. 2028 (Commencing 4 January 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within the School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering The Centre of Micro/nano Manufacturing Technology (www.mnmt-dublin.org) has been established at the University College Dublin (UCD) to deliver high-impact, innovative science and engineering research since 2016. MNMT- Dublin has particular focus on instruments development and high precision manufacturing combined with optical and bio-medical technologies applied in optical image, visual optics, and bio-medical implants. The Centre brings together a multi-disciplinary team of over 20 PhD and Post-Doc researchers in manufacturing engineering, instrumentation and optics, in fundamental and translational research. Project Description: High-precision manufacturing for optical and bio-medical applications is a government funded project primed to develop high-precision manufacturing technology for optical and bio-medical applications. The project scope covers ultra-precision machining, micro/nano fabrication and nanometric surface finishing. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020134": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 Oct. 2028 (Commencing 4 January 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 Oct. 2028 (Commencing 4 January 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within the School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering The Centre of Micro/nano Manufacturing Technology (www.mnmt-dublin.org) has been established at the University College Dublin (UCD) to deliver high-impact, innovative science and engineering research since 2016. MNMT- Dublin has particular focus on instruments development and high precision manufacturing combined with optical and bio-medical technologies applied in optical image, visual optics, and bio-medical implants. The Centre brings together a multi-disciplinary team of over 20 PhD and Post-Doc researchers in manufacturing engineering, instrumentation and optics, in fundamental and translational research. Project Description: High-precision manufacturing for optical and bio-medical applications is a government funded project primed to develop high-precision manufacturing technology for optical and bio-medical applications. The project scope covers ultra-precision machining, micro/nano fabrication and nanometric surface finishing. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020048": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The Chromatin Mechanisms in Disease laboratory (https://conwaychromatinlab.com/) at University College Dublin, led by Dr. Eric Conway, are recruiting a postdoctoral fellow to work on understanding the mechanisms through which the repressive histone modification H2AK119ub1 is dysregulated in disease. This position will be funded through a Wellcome Trust award. Histone H2A lysine 119 mono-ubiquitination (H2AK119ub1) is a repressive histone modification that is catalysed by the PRC1 complex and erased by the PR-DUB complex. Variants in critical subunits of each complex are known to be the causative event in diverse human diseases, such as AML and chromatinopathies. This project will investigate how pathogenic variants in members of the PRC1 and PR-DUB complexes contribute to changes in H2AK119ub1 using cancer and neurodevelopmental disease model systems. This will encompass a range of functional genomics, biochemistry and proteomics methods to investigate the precise impact that variants have on PR-DUB and PRC1 function – using methods such as CUT&Tag, Captify, RNA-seq, immunoprecipitation followed by mass spectrometry and high throughput pooled CRISPR screens. The role of the applicant will be either computational biology, wet-lab or a hybrid of both depending on the successful candidates expertise. There will be strong opportunities for continued professional development as part of UCD Research Careers Framework and through attendance at external training courses and conferences. The applicant will be strongly encouraged and supported to pursue external funding opportunities during the period of the appointment in line with the development of their own career prospects and to further the overall research activities of the group. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum PD2 Salary: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers who have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020062": {
      "title": "UCDVO Programme Assistant, UCD Global, Temporary 11 month post",
      "description": "UCDVO Programme Assistant, UCD Global, Temporary 11 month post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCDVO Programme Assistant within UCD Global . UCD Global steers and guides the global strategies of the university, providing expert leadership in partnerships and engagement, international student recruitment and support, inbound and outbound staff and student mobility, and the international elements of the student experience. Leveraging relationships with external stakeholders, UCD Global works at the interface of the university and the international community. It supports university leaders to shape policy, works with Colleges/Schools and other support units to ensure delivery, and liaises with students and staff to measure success and impact. Headquartered in Dublin, UCD Global also directs and manages the university’s network of Global Centres, which serve as hubs of UCD activity in North America, China, South Asia, Asia-Pacific and the Middle East. UCD Volunteers Overseas is located within UCD Global and provides opportunities for students, staff, faculty and alumni to engage in international volunteering and global citizenship education programmes. Volunteers engage in volunteering overseas/and/or virtually for four weeks each year to work on a broad range of community development projects carried out in partnership with NGOs, academic institutions and community groups. The UCDVO Programme Assistant will provide a high level of administrative and programme quality support for UCDVO’s volunteering and global citizenship programmes and contribute to the success of the new five year strategic plan 95 Executive Assistant_2013 (2010) Salary Scale: €32,856 - €49,419 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Cúntóir Cláir UCDVO laistigh de UCD Ar Fud na Cruinne. Cuirtear fáilte roimh iarratais ar phost mar Chúntóir Cláir UCDVO. Cuirfidh Cúntóir Cláir UCDVO tacaíocht ardleibhéil ar fáil maidir le cúrsaí riaracháin agus cáilíocht na gclár d’oibríochtaí deonacha agus do chláir saoránachta domhanda UCDVO, agus cuirfidh siad cuspóirí an phlean straitéisigh nua cúig bliana. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 09/10/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020094": {
      "title": "Venture - Facilitator, UCD Innovation Academy, 11 months Temporary Part-Time i.e. half-time / 0.5fte",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 Venture - Facilitator, UCD Innovation Academy, 11 months Temporary Part-Time i.e. half-time / 0.5fte Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Venture - Facilitator within the UCD Innovation Academy The UCD Innovation Academy creates transformational learning experiences to equip diverse learner cohorts with the forward-looking skills and attributes required for an increasingly complex world. We do this by taking an experiential approach to developing an entrepreneurial mindset for all – creating value, engaging others, and learning from trial and error. Tackling real world problems and engaging others outside the university is an integral part of all our programmes. If you have the professional experience to facilitate learning through exploration, without lecturing or relying on case studies, as well as the flexibility to work with ease in a multidisciplinary, multicultural and multigenerational environment, then we encourage you to apply. 95 Administrative Officer I (2013) Salary Scale: €53,976 - €72,929 per annum pro-rata Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach laistigh de UCD Innovation Academy Cruthaíonn Acadamh Nuálaíochta UCD eispéiris fhoghlama ar fáil a ullmhaíonn grúpaí éagsúla foghlaimeoirí leis na scileanna réamhbhreathnaitheacha a theastaíonn chun dul i ngleic le saol atá ag éirí níos casta le himeacht ama. Trí chur chuige bunaithe ar an taithí a ghlacadh, cothaímid meon fiontraíochta a fhorbairt do chách - luach a chruthú, daoine eile a mhealladh, agus foghlaim ó thriail agus earráid. Is cuid lárnach de gach clár a chuirimid ar fáil iad fadhbanna an tsaoil ​​a réiteach agus daoine eile lasmuigh den ollscoil a mhealladh. Má tá taithí ghairmiúil agat chun foghlaim trí thaiscéalaíocht a éascú, gan léachtóireacht a dhéanamh ná bheith ag brath ar chás-staidéir, chomh maith leis an tsolúbthacht chun oibriú gan stró i dtimpeallacht ildisciplíneach, ilchultúrtha agus ilghlúine, molaimid duit iarratas a dhéanamh. 95 Administrative Officer I (2013) Scála Tuarastail: €53,976 - €72,929 in aghaidh na bliana, pro-rata Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 9.10.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    }
  },
